## Recommended Tech Stack (Fixed to package.json)
### Frontend:
- **Framework:** Next.js 14 (App Router) + React 18 + TypeScript 5 — fits current project setup
- **Documentation:** Next.js (https://nextjs.org/docs), React (https://react.dev/), TypeScript (https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/)

### Backend/Cloud:
- **Amplify Gen 2:** for auth/data; local via Amplify Next.js sandbox; prod via Amplify hosting
- **Documentation:** Amplify Gen 2 (https://docs.amplify.aws/gen2/)

### Styling/UI:
- **Tailwind CSS v4:** utility-first styling; `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` for class composition
  - **CRITICAL:** When setting up Tailwind CSS v4, ensure:
    1. Install `@tailwindcss/postcss` package: `yarn add -D @tailwindcss/postcss`
    2. Use `@tailwindcss/postcss` in `postcss.config.js` (not `tailwindcss`)
    3. Use `@import 'tailwindcss';` in `globals.css` (not `@tailwind` directives)
    4. See [BUG-006](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/configuration/tailwind-css-v4-postcss-plugin-error.md) for details
- **lucide-react:** icon set per project convention (no emojis)
- **LiquidGlass system:** for elevated surfaces (cards/sheets/toolbars) use consistent glass classes and tokens; respect motion/accessibility rules and WCAG AA contrast.
- **Documentation:** Tailwind (https://tailwindcss.com/docs), lucide-react (https://lucide.dev/), tailwind-merge (https://github.com/dcastil/tailwind-merge)

### Validation:
- **Zod:** schema validation and type inference
- **Documentation:** https://zod.dev/

### Tooling/Infra:
- **TypeScript 5, esbuild, tsx, AWS CDK v2, constructs**
- **Documentation:** TypeScript (https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/), esbuild (https://esbuild.github.io/), tsx (https://github.com/esbuild-kit/tsx), AWS CDK (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/home.html)

### Electron/Desktop (if applicable):
- **Electron + Vite:** for cross-platform desktop apps
  - **CRITICAL:** When setting up electron-vite, ensure:
    1. Explicitly set `outDir` in `electron.vite.config.ts` for all build targets (main, preload, renderer)
    2. `outDir` must match the `package.json` `main` field path structure (e.g., `dist-electron/main`)
    3. Preload script paths in window configuration must match output structure (e.g., `../preload/index.js` for `dist-electron/main` → `dist-electron/preload`)
    4. Configure cache paths for Windows compatibility (before `app.whenReady()`):
       - Set `app.setPath('userCache', app.getPath('userData'))` for Windows
       - Set `app.setPath('sessionData', app.getPath('userData'))` for Windows
       - Handle cache permission errors gracefully (suppress non-critical errors)
    5. Set `cache: false` or `partition: 'persist:main'` in webPreferences for Windows
    6. **Filter macOS metadata files:** When implementing file scanning/processing, always filter out macOS resource fork/metadata files (files starting with `._`) to prevent "Unknown file format" errors during EXIF extraction and thumbnail generation. Use `isMacOSMetadataFile()` helper function in file type checks. See [BUG-009](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/macos-metadata-file-exif-extraction-error.md) for details
    7. **Use HashRouter for Electron apps (MUST):** Always use `HashRouter` (never `BrowserRouter`) for Electron renderers. Enable React Router future flags. Encode file-path IDs before placing in URLs (e.g., base64url). See [BUG-011](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/photo-id-routing-error.md)
      8. **Register custom protocol for local files:** Never use `file://` URLs in the renderer process. Instead, register a custom protocol handler (e.g., `atlas-photo://`) to serve thumbnails and photos securely. See [BUG-010](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/thumbnail-file-protocol-loading-error.md) for details
    9. **Never use Node.js APIs in renderer process:** Never use Node.js APIs (like `Buffer`, `fs`, `path`) directly in the renderer process. Use browser-compatible APIs (TextEncoder, TextDecoder, btoa, atob) for encoding/decoding. Create utility functions for browser-compatible operations. See [BUG-012](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/buffer-not-defined-renderer-error.md) for details
    10. **Custom protocol registration (MUST):** Register protocols before creating `BrowserWindow`. If using a custom partition, register on that session via `session.fromPartition(...).protocol.registerFileProtocol()` and unregister first if needed; also register on default session as fallback. Disable sandbox (`sandbox: false`) only if required by protocol constraints. See [BUG-013](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/custom-protocol-not-registered-error.md)
    11. **Renderer CSP (MUST):** Set a Content-Security-Policy on the renderer session in development (allow HMR) and tighten for production. See [BUG-015](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/electron-content-security-policy-warning.md)
    12. Always test `yarn electron:dev` after setup to catch output directory mismatches and cache errors early
    13. See [BUG-007](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/configuration/electron-vite-output-directory-mismatch-error.md), [BUG-008](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/electron-cache-permission-error.md), [BUG-009](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/macos-metadata-file-exif-extraction-error.md), [BUG-010](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/thumbnail-file-protocol-loading-error.md), [BUG-011](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/photo-id-routing-error.md), [BUG-012](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/buffer-not-defined-renderer-error.md), [BUG-013](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/custom-protocol-not-registered-error.md), and [BUG-015](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/electron-content-security-policy-warning.md) for details
  - **Documentation:** Electron (https://www.electronjs.org/docs/), electron-vite (https://electron-vite.org/)

