## Authoring Standards and Coding Conventions

- Functional React only (no classes) to match team preference.
- Document complex functions with TSDoc/JSDoc (`/** ... */`) including params/returns, side effects, and assumptions.
- Keep variable and function names descriptive (no abbreviations); prefer readability over brevity.
- Do not remove existing functionality during refactors; maintain backward compatibility.

### React Router Configuration (BUG-014)
- **CRITICAL:** When using React Router v6, always enable future flags to prepare for v7 migration and suppress warnings:
  ```typescript
  <HashRouter
    future={{
      v7_startTransition: true,
      v7_relativeSplatPath: true,
    }}
  >
    <App />
  </HashRouter>
  ```
- See [BUG-014](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/general/react-router-future-flag-warnings.md) for details.

### Electron Content-Security-Policy (BUG-015)
- **CRITICAL:** Always configure Content-Security-Policy for Electron renderer processes to prevent security warnings:
  ```typescript
  mainWindow.webContents.session.webRequest.onHeadersReceived(
    (details, callback) => {
      callback({
        responseHeaders: {
          ...details.responseHeaders,
          'Content-Security-Policy': [
            "default-src 'self'; " +
              "script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'; " +
              "style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; " +
              "img-src 'self' data: atlas-photo: file:; " +
              "font-src 'self' data:; " +
              "connect-src 'self' http://localhost:* ws://localhost:* ws://127.0.0.1:*;",
          ],
        },
      });
    }
  );
  ```
- Development mode requires `unsafe-eval` for Vite HMR; production should use stricter policies.
- See [BUG-015](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/electron/electron-content-security-policy-warning.md) for details.

### Component Import Verification (BUG-016)
- **CRITICAL:** Always verify all component imports when adding new UI components:
  - When adding component usage, immediately add the import statement
  - Use TypeScript strict mode to catch missing imports
  - Test loading states to ensure all components are imported
  - Create a checklist: "Verify all component imports when adding new UI components"
- See [BUG-016](../../Docs/Bug_Reports/ui-ux/skeleton-component-not-imported-error.md) for details.


